==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|extricatio|lang=la}} < {{term|extrico|extricō|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{audio|en-us-extricate.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|extricat|ing}}
#{{transitive}} To [[free]], [[disengage]], [[loosen]], or [[untangle]].
#:''I finally managed to '''extricate''' myself from the tight jacket.''
# {{rare}} To free from [[intricacy|intricacies]] or [[perplexity]]
#*'''1662:''' Thomas Salusbury, ''Galileo's Dialogue Concerning the Two Chief World Systems'' (Dialogue Two)
#*:''Your argumentation ... is invelloped with certain intricacies, that are not easie to be '''extricated'''.''

